From c6578263fbdc2e2c20e56237ef7c66997b4ec312 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:49:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 37/39] drama: long-form cuts the fewest balanced segments
 where the text turns

Segments default to 500 characters. A long input is cut into the fewest
segments that fit, at sentence ends only (inside a sentence only when it
alone is too long), choosing the cuts that minimize the segments' relative
deviation from the mean length less a bonus for each cut where the text
turns: a blank line, a question, or a sentence opening a new move (So,
Okay, OK, Now, Right, Anyway, Also, Next, Finally, But, Here's, or a
number and thing(s)). Such a cut rests 0.60 s; a blank line keeps 0.70 s.
Each join's pitch resets with the new turn, so fewer joins, placed at
turns, leave fewer resets to hear.
